==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|premunires}}

# The [[offense]] under English law of appealing to or obeying a foreign court or authority, thus challenging the supremacy of the Crown. 
#*'''1724''', Johnatan Swift, ''[[s:The Works of the Rev. Jonathan Swift|The Works of the Rev. Jonathan Swift]]'', Volume 9, [[s:The Works of the Rev. Jonathan Swift/Volume 9/The Drapier’s Letters 5|The Drapier’s Letters 5]]:
#*: For I have heard of a judge, who upon the criminal's appeal to the dreadful day of judgment, told him, he had incurred a '''premunire''', for appealing to a foreign jurisdiction; and of another in Wales, who severely checked the prisoner for offering the same plea; [..]
# The [[writ]] charging this offense. 
# The [[penalty]] for this offense.

